    "prose": "Rain drummed harder beyond the covered yard, and the wind pushed damp air across the level ramp. Aya and Mert kept their shared hold on the restored mosaic panel. It remained level and intact between them.\n\nAya looked along the covered route to the open gallery door. Her arms were beginning to ache, but rushing now would only make the fragile panel harder to control.\n\n“Mert, can we carry it more slowly on the ramp?” she asked. “I need us to keep the same pace.”\n\nMert heard her request and met her eyes. He gave a short nod. “Yes. You set the first step, and I’ll match you.”\n\nAya moved one foot forward without advancing onto the ramp. Mert adjusted his stance to the same measured rhythm, clearly slowing his movements to match the pace she had requested. Aya watched him settle into it. The pull on her side eased, and the mosaic stayed even.\n\n“Like that,” she said.\n\n“Like that,” Mert agreed.\n\nStill supporting their opposite sides, Aya and Mert carried the same fragile panel together along the level covered ramp from the covered yard to the gallery entry, maintaining their shared hold for the entire crossing.\n\nRain beat against the covered route, louder now, but neither of them hurried. At the gallery entry, they stopped together before the wide open door. The panel remained raised between them, restored and intact.\n\nAya released a careful breath. “That was better.”\n\nMert glanced at the even edge of the mosaic. “Slower was better.”\n\nThey stayed at the entry with both of them still carrying it. Beyond the open door, the fixed display mount waited in the alcove, but they did not take the panel inside yet.",
